# Android Kotlin conventions

- Kotlin only. Prefer Jetpack Compose and Material 3 for UI.
- Keep screen state in a ViewModel; expose immutable UI state.
- Prefer Coroutines and Flow for asynchronous work.
- Prefer sealed types over nullable values for parse/resolve results.
- Prefer Android standard APIs and stable Jetpack libraries.
- Prefer minimal dependencies. Use Kotlin DSL (`*.gradle.kts`).
- Do not introduce repositories, DI frameworks, or extra layers unless they
  solve a concrete problem already present in the code.
- Keep functions small and purpose-specific. Prefer boring, readable code.
